            <title>[IGNITE-2833] High memory utilization when OFFHEAP_TIERED mode and expiry policy are enabled.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2833</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The problem is originally reported by Neil Wightman: &lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-users.70518.x6.nabble.com/Off-Heap-cache-using-lots-of-heap-memory-td3414.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-users.70518.x6.nabble.com/Off-Heap-cache-using-lots-of-heap-memory-td3414.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Steps to reproduce&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
1) Run attached code and XML config. Observe that heap size is about 1Gb.&lt;br/&gt;
2) Comment expiry policy setter in the code, run again. Now only 150Mb is consumed.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
